  "term": "circadian rhythm sleep disorder",
  "definition": "Circadian rhythm sleep disorder is a sleep problem in which the usual 24-hour sleep-wake pattern is disrupted. It can occur in connection with travel, shift work, or other causes that disturb normal timing of sleep.",
